            <ArticleTitle>Cranial arteritis mimicking odontogenic pain: report of case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>621-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 65-year-old patient treated for pain of apparent odontogenic origin did not respond to appropriate dental treatment. While the signs and symptoms mimicked a dental problem, further diagnostic evaluation determined the &quot;culprit&quot;--cranial arteritis. Proper treatment immediately after diagnosis is advised as the complications of cranial arteritis can include the rapid onset of blindness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
